 left side. How many squares are shaded altogether?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O2", "skill": "Application", "pts": 1, "sec": "A · Fluency", "unit": "squares", "units": ["squares"]}, {"id": "m5u02v3Aq08", "type": "num", "prompt": "Three straws, each 5 cm long, make a triangle. What is the total length of straw used?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "pts": 1, "sec": "A · Fluency", "unit": "cm", "units": ["cm"]}, {"id": "m5u02v3Aq09", "type": "short", "prompt": "The y-axis is a mirror line. Point A is at (5, −3). Write the coordinates of its reflection.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O2", "skill": "Figure", "pts": 1, "fig": {"kind": "coord", "x": [-6, 6], "y": [-6, 6], "points": [{"x": 5, "y": -3, "l": "A"}]}, "sec": "B · Methods"}, {"id": "m5u02v3Aq10", "type": "grid", "prompt": "Sort the triangles by their side lengths.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Data", "pts": 2, "sec": "B · Methods", "cols": ["scalene", "isosceles", "equilateral"], "mode": "classify", "rows": [{"l": "7 cm, 6 cm, 8 cm"}, {"l": "5 cm, 5 cm, 3 cm"}, {"l": "7 cm, 6 cm, 8 cm"}, {"l": "3 cm, 7 cm, 8 cm"}]}, {"id": "m5u02v3Aq11", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "Which shape always has exactly one line of symmetry?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O2", "skill": "Reasoning", "pts": 1, "sec": "B · Methods", "options": [{"t": "rectangle"}, {"t": "square"}, {"t": "kite"}, {"t": "equilateral triangle"}]}, {"id": "m5u02v3Aq12", "type": "num", "prompt": "A tile pattern looks the same when folded along 3 different lines. How many lines of symmetry does it have?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O2", "skill": "Application", "pts": 1, "sec": "B · Methods", "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "bare": true}, {"id": "m5u02v3Aq13", "type": "num", "prompt": "A square on a grid is 3 squares to the right of a vertical mirror line. How many squares to the left of the line is its reflection?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O2", "skill": "Application", "pts": 1, "sec": "B · Methods", "unit": "squares", "units": ["squares"]}, {"id": "m5u02v3Aq14", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "A road sign is a triangle with all sides equal. How many lines of symmetry does it have?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O2", "skill": "Reasoning", "pts": 1, "sec": "B · Methods", "options": [{"t": "3"}, {"t": "6"}, {"t": "1"}, {"t": "0"}]}, {"id": "m5u02v3Aq15", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "Lucy cuts a rectangle 5 cm by 6 cm along a diagonal. What type of triangles does she get?", "diff": "H", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "pts": 1, "sec": "C · Problem solving", "options": [{"t": "right-angled isosceles triangles"}, {"t": "equilateral triangles"}, {"t": "right-angled scalene triangles"}]}, {"id": "m5u02v3Aq16", "type": "grid", "prompt": "Is each statement about triangles always, sometimes or never true?", "diff": "H", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Data", "pts": 1, "sec": "C · Problem solving", "cols": ["Sometimes true", "Never true", "Always true"], "mode": "classify", "rows": [{"l": "An isosceles triangle has a right angle"}, {"l": "A triangle has four sides"}, {"l": "A scalene triangle has two equal sides"}, {"l": "An equilateral triangle has three equal angles"}]}, {"id": "m5u02v3Aq17", "type": "num", "prompt": "An isosceles triangle has a perimeter of 36 cm. Its odd side is 6 cm. How long is each equal side?", "diff": "H", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "pts": 2, "sec": "C · Problem solving", "unit": "cm", "units": ["cm"]}, {"id": "m5u02v3Aq18", "type": "num", "prompt": "An isosceles triangle has a perimeter of 18 cm. Its shortest side is 4 cm and the other two are equal. How long is each equal side?", "diff": "H", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "pts": 1, "sec": "C · Problem solving", "unit": "cm", "units": ["cm"]}, {"id": "m5u02v3Aq19", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "Kiran draws a triangle with angles 40°, 40° and 100°. What type of triangle is it?", "diff": "H", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "pts": 1, "sec": "C · Problem solving", "options": [{"t": "equilateral"}, {"t": "isosceles"}, {"t": "scalene"}]}, {"id": "m5u02v3Aq20", "type": "num", 